Approach 3 — Recursive k-Group Reversal

This is the clean recursive approach.

Core Idea

For:

1 → 2 → 3 → 4 → 5
k = 2

First reverse:

1 → 2

into:

2 → 1

Then recursively process:

3 → 4 → 5

which becomes:

4 → 3 → 5

Final:

2 → 1 → 4 → 3 → 5

Code
class Solution {

    public ListNode reverseKGroup(ListNode head, int k) {

        // Check whether k nodes are available
        ListNode temp = head;

        for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {
            if (temp == null) {
                return head;
            }
            temp = temp.next;
        }

        // Reverse first k nodes
        ListNode curr = head;
        ListNode prev = null;

        for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {
            ListNode next = curr.next;

            curr.next = prev;
            prev = curr;
            curr = next;
        }

        // head is now the last node of reversed group
        head.next = reverseKGroup(curr, k);

        return prev;
    }
}

